 "missing_en": "No page we read shows organised transport or a named travel contact for Kymenlaakso lung cancer patients going to HUS.",
 "summary_en": "HUS's patient leaflet (approved 21.07.2025) says the treating unit books the patient hotel at Scandic Meilahti and the patient pays nothing beyond the hospital fee. Kymenlaakso's own site says radiotherapy is given at Kymenlaakso Central Hospital in Kotka, so the travel problem is mainly surgery in Helsinki. The only effect evidence is an English registry study (Crawford 2009, British Journal of Cancer): patients with the longest travel time had 0.60 times the odds of lung cancer surgery, which is an association, not a test of travel support.",
